{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"Five of seven groups already pass. The remaining valid-path failure was a test-construction issue: `center + radius` followed by subtraction is not always an exact floating boundary, so I’m constructing boundary circles at the origin. The invalid enum exposes the C function’s undefined fallthrough returning the caller’s incoming `EAX`; I’m adding a small x86_64 FFI trampoline that pins `EAX=0` for both calls, giving the same concrete external-call condition and exact result."}}
